IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc4-attendance-allowance`
IMPORT `ssc4-disability-living-allowance`

-- TESTS for ssc4-disability-living-allowance.l4 (ss 71-76). Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- ss 71 to 76`

§§ `s 71`

#ASSERT `s 71(1) the component is part of disability living allowance` `s 71(1) care component` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(1) the component is part of disability living allowance` `s 71(1) mobility component` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(1) the component is part of disability living allowance` `s 71(1) another component` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 71(2) the person's entitlement to disability living allowance is an entitlement to the components` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(2) the person's entitlement to disability living allowance is an entitlement to the components` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(2) the person's entitlement to disability living allowance is an entitlement to the components` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(2) the person's entitlement to disability living allowance is an entitlement to the components` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 71(3): both components for different fixed periods: JUST FALSE. One component, any term: JUST TRUE. Both for the same fixed period, both indefinite, or one fixed and one indefinite: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 71(3) the terms of the award are permitted` TRUE (`s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` (Date 31 12 2026)) TRUE (`s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` (Date 31 12 2027)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 71(3) the terms of the award are permitted` TRUE (`s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` (Date 31 12 2026)) TRUE (`s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` (Date 31 12 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 71(3) the terms of the award are permitted` TRUE `s 71(3) an indefinite period` TRUE `s 71(3) an indefinite period` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 71(3) the terms of the award are permitted` TRUE (`s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` (Date 31 12 2026)) TRUE `s 71(3) an indefinite period` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 71(3) the terms of the award are permitted` TRUE (`s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` (Date 31 12 2026)) FALSE `s 71(3) an indefinite period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(3) the terms of the award are permitted` FALSE `s 71(3) an indefinite period` TRUE (`s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` (Date 31 12 2027)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(3) the terms of the award are permitted` FALSE `s 71(3) an indefinite period` FALSE `s 71(3) an indefinite period` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 71(4) and (5): the rates are inputs (84.7 and 59.3 are test numbers only).
#ASSERT `s 71(4) the weekly rate of the disability living allowance for a week with one component in pounds` (JUST 84.7) EQUALS JUST 84.7
#ASSERT `s 71(4) the weekly rate of the disability living allowance for a week with one component in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 71(5) the weekly rate of the disability living allowance for a week with both components in pounds` (JUST 84.7) (JUST 59.3) EQUALS JUST 144
#ASSERT `s 71(5) the weekly rate of the disability living allowance for a week with both components in pounds` NOTHING (JUST 59.3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 71(5) the weekly rate of the disability living allowance for a week with both components in pounds` (JUST 84.7) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 71(6) and (7).
#ASSERT `s 71(6) the person is barred from a disability living allowance by the residence and presence conditions` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 71(6) the person is barred from a disability living allowance by the residence and presence conditions` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(6) the person is barred from a disability living allowance by the residence and presence conditions` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 71(7) the person is barred from a disability living allowance while entitled to a Scottish or pension age payment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(7) the person is barred from a disability living allowance while entitled to a Scottish or pension age payment` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(7) the person is barred from a disability living allowance while entitled to a Scottish or pension age payment` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(7) the person is barred from a disability living allowance while entitled to a Scottish or pension age payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 71(7) the person is barred from a disability living allowance while entitled to a Scottish or pension age payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 72 -- the care component`

-- Fixtures: the six limbs (a)(i), (a)(ii), (b)(i), (b)(ii), (c)(i), (c)(ii).
`s 72(1) test facts attention only` MEANS `s 72(1) Care component facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 72(1) test facts cooked meal only` MEANS `s 72(1) Care component facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 72(1) test facts day supervision only` MEANS `s 72(1) Care component facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 72(1) test facts night watching only` MEANS `s 72(1) Care component facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s 72(1) test facts none` MEANS `s 72(1) Care component facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- s 72(1A): without (b)(i) or (ii) the conditions are not taken to be satisfied (FALSE); with one of them and a limb other than the cooked-meal one, TRUE; the cooked-meal limb alone is disregarded, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 72(1A) the conditions in subsection (1) are satisfied as modified for the part of a period before he reaches 16` `s 72(1) test facts attention only` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 72(1A) the conditions in subsection (1) are satisfied as modified for the part of a period before he reaches 16` `s 72(1) test facts attention only` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(1A) the conditions in subsection (1) are satisfied as modified for the part of a period before he reaches 16` `s 72(1) test facts attention only` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(1A) the conditions in subsection (1) are satisfied as modified for the part of a period before he reaches 16` `s 72(1) test facts cooked meal only` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 72(1A) the conditions in subsection (1) are satisfied as modified for the part of a period before he reaches 16` `s 72(1) test facts night watching only` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 72(1): a person over 16 on the day (under 16 is JUST FALSE) with any one limb: entitled; with none: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts attention only` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts cooked meal only` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts day supervision only` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts night watching only` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts none` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under 16: the cooked-meal limb does not apply (NOTHING); attention needs the extra proof; with proof, TRUE.
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts cooked meal only` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts attention only` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts attention only` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts attention only` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Age unknown: the modified conditions decide where they are met (TRUE); the cooked-meal limb alone is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts attention only` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `s 72(1) test facts cooked meal only` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 72(2): the award would begin on 1 July 2025. The 3 months immediately preceding begin on 1 April 2025; the 6 months beginning with the award date end on 31 December 2025.
-- (a) boundary: a run beginning 1 April 2025 meets (a); 2 April does not (and no prescribed other period is known: NOTHING; known not satisfied: bar).
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 2 4 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 2 4 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 2 4 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) boundary: the run must reach 31 December 2025; 30 December is one day short (bar). Death expected within the 6 months shortens it to the day of death.
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 30 12 2025) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 15 8 2025) (JUST (Date 15 8 2025)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 14 8 2025) (JUST (Date 15 8 2025)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) (JUST (Date 31 12 2025)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Death expected after the 6 months: not "within" them, so the 6 months still apply.
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 30 12 2025) (JUST (Date 1 1 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A month-end award date: 31 August less 3 months is "31 May" (exists) but six months on is "31 February": NOTHING (fork F2).
#ASSERT `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` (Date 31 8 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2026) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 72(2A).
#ASSERT `s 72(2A) the modifications in subsection (1A) have effect for subsection (2) on the day` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(2A) the modifications in subsection (1A) have effect for subsection (2) on the day` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 72(2A) the modifications in subsection (1A) have effect for subsection (2) on the day` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 72(2A) the modifications in subsection (1A) have effect for subsection (2) on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 72(4): highest if both (b) and (c) throughout both periods; middle if one or other; lowest in any other case. Test rates 90, 60, 25 (inputs).
#ASSERT `s 72(4) the weekly rate of the care component in pounds` TRUE TRUE (JUST 90) (JUST 60) (JUST 25) EQUALS JUST 90
#ASSERT `s 72(4) the weekly rate of the care component in pounds` FALSE TRUE (JUST 90) (JUST 60) (JUST 25) EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `s 72(4) the weekly rate of the care component in pounds` FALSE FALSE (JUST 90) (JUST 60) (JUST 25) EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `s 72(4) the weekly rate of the care component in pounds` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST 60) (JUST 25) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 72(5)(a): the later of 3 months before the claim and the first date terminally ill. Claim 10 September 2025: 10 June 2025.
#ASSERT `s 72(5)(a) the first day of the period for which the person is taken to have satisfied the conditions` (Date 10 9 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 6 2025)
